{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\fs22 The Importance of Creating a Project in the CRM to Track a Transaction\line \line Creating a project in the CRM (Customer Relationship Management) system to track a transaction is essential for maintaining visibility, organization, and accountability throughout the lifecycle of a deal. Heres why it's important:\line \line -\line Centralized Information\line A project entry consolidates all relevant details  including client data, transaction documents, communications, timelines, and milestones  in one accessible location. This eliminates confusion and ensures everyone is working with the same information.\line \line -\line Improved Communication\line With a project in place, internal teams and external stakeholders can be updated in real-time. It reduces the risk of miscommunication and keeps all parties aligned with progress and expectations.\line \line -\line Efficient Workflow Management\line CRM projects allow for task assignments, deadline tracking, and workflow automation. This ensures the transaction is progressing as planned and bottlenecks are quickly addressed.\line \line -\line Transparency and Accountability\line Every action taken on a transaction is logged in the project record. This promotes responsibility, enhances internal accountability, and simplifies audits or reporting requirements.\line \line -\line Performance Tracking and Reporting\line Projects within the CRM allow you to track key metrics, monitor progress, and generate detailed reports. This supports informed decision-making and helps refine processes over time.\line \line -\line Regulatory Compliance\line Many financial transactions require documentation for KYC, AML, and audit purposes. A properly maintained CRM project ensures these compliance records are readily available and up-to-date.\line \line -\line Client Trust and Satisfaction\line Structured tracking and timely updates reflect professionalism and build trust with clients, demonstrating that their transaction is being handled with care and transparency.\line \line Once the Project is Created:\line \line -\line Assign the Designated Trustees\line Allocate the appropriate trustees to oversee and manage the project.\line \line -\line Initiate Communication\line Maintain an open line of communication to ensure all team members are aligned on objectives and expectations.\line \line -\line Notify Relevant Parties\line Inform all relevant stakeholders that the project has been initiated and provide them with access as needed.\line \line -\line Launch the Task List\line Begin populating and executing the project task list to maintain momentum and structure.\line \line -\line Establish a Collaborative Group\line Create a dedicated communication group that includes the client and assigned trustees for efficient updates and coordination.\line \line Please use the portal for all communication aside from pre-planned meetings.\line \line Thank you,\line US Capital Private Bank Client Relations}